'''Gilman station''' is an [[Amtrak]] intercity train station in [[Gilman, Illinois]], United States. The stop is on their ''[[Illini and Saluki]]'' route.

Service began at Gilman on October 26, 1986, when the ''Illini'' began stopping there. It was the first passenger service at Gilman since the creation of Amtrak on May 1, 1971. The northbound ''[[City of New Orleans (train)|City of New Orleans]]'' also served Gilman until November 10, 1996.<ref>{{Sanders-Heartland}}</ref>{{rp|105}} The previous railroad station in Gilman was in the center of the city, located at the [[Level junction|diamond junction]] between Illinois Central's main line to [[New Orleans]] and the [[Toledo, Peoria and Western Railway]] (TP&W). The northwest quadrant of the junction contained the Illinois Central's main line to [[Springfield, IL|Springfield]] and [[St Louis]], which split with the New Orleans main line just north of the station. The station building is still standing and is used by the [[Canadian National Railway]]'s engineering department.<ref>{{cite book|title=Outside the Rails: A Rail Route Guide from Chicago to Carbondale, IL|author1=Robert Tabern|author2=Kandace Tabern|date=February 1, 2017|page=55}}</ref>

